resources: the density contract (value rows, raster files, colour aliases)

Three gaps in how the resource layer treats density and references, all
measured on Instagram 455 installed as base.apk + split_config.xxhdpi.apk and
shown on a 160 dpi window.

1. A density qualifier on a VALUE row is ranked, not dropped
   (ResourceIndex, MACAPK_RES_VALUE_DENSITY, default on). AOSP never eliminates
   a config by density. `dimen/tab_bar_height_panorama` exists only as
   `-xxhdpi = 48dp`; the theme binds ?attr/tabBarHeight to it, so the bottom
   tab bar was laid out 0 px tall and a window narrower than 600 dp had no
   navigation at all.

2. A raster resource is scaled from its file's bucket to the display's
   (Resources / BitmapFactory, MACAPK_RES_BITMAP_DENSITY, default on):
   ResourceIndex.macapkFileDensity reports the selected file row's density,
   getDrawable decodes with inDensity/inTargetDensity, a compiled 9-patch has
   its divs and padding scaled with AOSP's scaleNinePatchChunk rounding,
   openRawResource(id, value) and getValue fill TypedValue.density, and
   BitmapFactory.decodeResource takes AOSP's decodeResourceStream route. The
   split ships 3,227 rasters (71 nine-patches), all drawn at 3x: a 92x96 dp
   "more" button, a 72 dp Reels tab icon among 24 dp siblings. Only a file
   whose config names a real bucket is scaled, so a run at the display's own
   bucket is byte-identical.

3. A colour alias whose target is a FILE reaches it (ResourceIndex ingest):
   `color/igds_prism_secondary_button_background_filled` ->
   `..._filled_dark` (res/gt.xml, a state list) missed, and the profile's
   "Edit profile" / "Share profile" buttons painted no background.

Applies to vendor/macapk at 57c9912 with `patch -p1` from vendor/macapk.

